      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "## Capacity campaign control\nPostgreSQL logical schema/table snapshots run every **5 minutes** with **30-day** retention. Container CPU, memory, PIDs, and Docker engine-storage capacity run every **15 seconds** into Loki with **7-day** local retention.\n\n**Authority matters:** on native Linux the engine filesystem is the storage authority. On Docker Desktop/WSL it is only the virtual guest; run `scripts/reporting/host_capacity_sampler.ps1` on Windows for the physical backing-volume panels and projections. The agent discovers Docker's configured VHDX path—no drive is hardcoded.\n\nSuggested first alerts: authoritative free space below the reserve; projected days to reserve below the response horizon; sustained DB/table growth above budget; connections above 70%; cache hit below 95%; or a collector above its measured CPU envelope.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "How to use this dashboard",
      "type": "text"
    },
